# s72_ideas.oot — Idea Fairy 🧚 residual 7.2 CRIT last-arg slice (path-A)
# Date: 2026-08-12
# Role: creative but **shippable** residual ideas — **no product code** this pass
# Audience: Domain Experts (implement winner) · peers (smoke / quote-depth) · Memory
# Scope: `c_sys_exec_last_arg` 7.2 close + 7.10 leftover concat helper — **not** M1–M20, not full IFC
## Problem (tree truth)
| Fact | Evidence |
|------|----------|
| Sprint pin | `SPRINT.oot` 7.2 CRIT: `c_sys_exec_last_arg` **same** as 7.1 (was “stack buffer / no per-char OoStr”) |
| Wording is stale | `.oo` has **no** C `char[]`. Memory already: 7.2 style = **one `str_slice` for the last top-level span** (`audit/t1_memory.oot` M-SG3) |
| Walker exists | `ooda/oodac/c_emit_args.oo` `c_sys_exec_last_arg` L71–129 — linear C-arg walk; skip `"..."` + `\\`; depth on `(`/`)`; top-level `,` updates `last_start` (skip spaces); **one** `str_slice(args, last_start, n)` |
| Call site | `c_secret_emit_guard` sys_exec branch: `last = c_sys_exec_last_arg(args)` then refuse only if `c_arg_is_cap_ident(last)` (`c_emit_secret_guard.oo` L130–140) |
| Not an ident walker | Last-arg is a **comma span** (may be a call, lit, or IDENT). Ident-slice helper does **not** replace this function |
| Twin walkers | `c_count_top_args` copies the same quote/escape/depth machine. `c_args_drop_first` is sliced but **not** string-aware |
| 7.1 already closed | Path-A FIXED (`str_slice` + `s71_guard_scan_smoke`); handoff said 7.2/7.10 next (`audit/s71_phalanx_rollup.oot`) |
| 7.10 still leaks | `c_parse_secret_env` still `name = name + c` per ident char (`c_emit_secret.oo` ~L60) — HIGH leftover concat |
| Shared oracles | Alpha-class copies in 7.1 walker + 7.10 name loop. Quote skip copies in last-arg + `c_count_top_args` + 7.1 |
| Handoff | `audit/shutdown_handoff_2026-08-12_r2_swarm.oot`: 7.2 “str_slice claimed; **needs prove/close only?**” |
| Existing fixtures | `secret_sys_exec_{fail,pass}.oo` (last IDENT vs last lit); `secret_sys_exec_argv_{fail,pass}.oo` (mid-argv; **not** last-span). Wired in `secret_sink_enforce_smoke.oo` / T2 depth |
| Dual path | Check/emit token walk: `c_secret_scan_call(..., want=1, eq_only=false)` refuses **any** argv IDENT after cap. Emit last-arg is a **belt** for last bare IDENT after lower |

**Not this wave:** full IFC, argv lattice, token-stream-only emit, rewriting `oo_sys_exec` ABI, C stack buffers, M1–M20.

## Constraints (hard)
1. **Path A only** — last-arg heap + quote/depth honesty, not “perfect argv taint.”
2. **Do not greenwash 7.2 from comments.** Close only on **static slice proof + quote/depth smoke**.
3. **Last-arg is a comma span.** Do not rewrite it into `c_slice_ident_at`. Shared ident helper **owns 7.10**.
4. **Keep dual-path honesty.** Token IDENT walk still covers mid-argv (`secret_sys_exec_argv_fail`). Last-arg is not a substitute.
5. **SPRINT “stack buffer” is not implementable in `.oo`.** Same as 7.1 — do not emit C `char buf[N]`.
6. **Reuse fixtures.** Prefer wiring `secret_sys_exec_*` + a **small** quote/depth TMPDIR matrix (s71 smoke shape).
7. **Line pressure** — helper ≤ existing `c_emit_args.oo` / `c_emit_secret.oo`. No new monofile.
8. **Fairy writes ideas only** — DE owns land + prove.

## Darwin scorecard (path-A residual)
Axes 0–10 (higher = survives compile cycle). Sum/5 ≈ rank:

| Axis | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Close** | Moves 7.2 CRIT (unproved slice / quote-depth FN) or 7.10 leftover concat |
| **Honest** | Named residual; no “stack buffer shipped”; last-span vs mid-argv not conflated |
| **Smoke** | Cheap pass+fail: last IDENT refuse, last lit allow, quote comma, nested depth |
| **Entropy** | Lowers \(S\) (untested 7.2 FIXED, concat copies, skip-machine drift) |
| **Ship** | ≤ few small edits + smoke; uses existing walker / fixtures |

**Rule:** losers pruned. 1–2 winners advance to DE this sprint turn.

---

## Ideas evaluated
### I1 — Prove/close 7.2 as **already sliced** (no last-arg rewrite) ⭐
**Shape:** Treat 7.2 product code as landed (`str_slice` once at end; no `out = out + char_at` in the walker). Close the CRIT with:
1. Static grep: `c_sys_exec_last_arg` contains `str_slice`; **no** per-char rebuild of the last span.
2. Immune smoke (I2) on last IDENT / last lit / quote comma / nested depth.
3. Rewrite SPRINT 7.2 line from “same” → **FIXED path-A (slice + prove)** after host smoke 0.
4. Named residual: last-arg is still a **re-lexer** of lowered C args; mid-argv remains token-walk (`c_secret_scan_call` want≥1).

**Smoke:** I2 matrix.
**Darwin:** Close 9 · Honest 10 · Smoke 9 · Entropy 9 · Ship 10 → **avg 9.4**
**Why winner-class:** Same “prove/close only?” as 7.1. Tree matches `t1_memory.oot` M-SG3. Avoids thrash rewrite of a working belt.

### I2 — Quote / depth **edge matrix** (7.2 prove rail) ⭐
**Shape:** One small script (`scripts/s72_last_arg_smoke.oo`, s71 TMPDIR shape) **or** a short addendum on `secret_sink_enforce_smoke.oo`. Dual-path `emit-c` where cheap. Do **not** invent a second product last-arg.

| Case | Fixture | Expect | Why |
|------|---------|--------|-----|
| Last IDENT refuse | `secret_sys_exec_fail.oo` (exists) | REFUSE `ERR\tsecret` | Last span is bare `token` + `c_arg_is_cap_ident` |
| Last lit allow | `secret_sys_exec_pass.oo` (exists) | ALLOW | Last is `"true"` — not cap IDENT |
| Mid-argv still refuse | `secret_sys_exec_argv_fail.oo` (exists) | REFUSE | **Token walk**, not last-arg (last is `"true"`). Prove dual-path; do not claim last-arg did this |
| Mid-argv clean | `secret_sys_exec_argv_pass.oo` (exists) | ALLOW | No secret IDENT in argv |
| Quote comma (no split) | TMPDIR: `sys_exec(sys, "echo", "a,b,c")` + unused `// SECRET: token` | ALLOW | Commas inside `"..."` must not move `last_start` |
| Quote comma + last IDENT | TMPDIR: `sys_exec(sys, "echo", "a,b", token)` | REFUSE | After string, last top-level span is `token` |
| Escape + quote | TMPDIR: last lit `"x\\\"y,z"` unused secret | ALLOW | `\\` then `"` must stay in-string so `,` is not top-level |
| Nested depth | TMPDIR: last is `helper(a, b)` unused secret | ALLOW (last-arg) | Inner `,` at depth>0 must not become last span; last is a **call** → `c_arg_is_cap_ident` false |
| Nested secret residual | TMPDIR: `sys_exec(sys, "echo", wrap(token))` | REFUSE **or named residual** | Last-arg will **not** see inner IDENT. Token walk may. **Do not soft-OK** if both miss |
| Empty / single span | TMPDIR or static: `args=""` → `"oo_str_lit(\"\")"`; no comma → whole `args` | structural | Empty fallback already in fn |
| Trailing comma | TMPDIR or grep-doc | last empty → return `args`; cap-ident false | Avoid FN theater; name the fallback |
| Static 7.2 | grep walker | `str_slice` present; no per-char last-span concat |

**Prefer ephemeral TMPDIR** for new quote/depth cases (s71 style) — do not grow fixture theater.

**Darwin:** Close 9 · Honest 10 · Smoke 10 · Entropy 10 · Ship 9 → **avg 9.6** (rails; not a solo product rewrite)
**Why must-bundle:** Without this, “7.2 FIXED” is comment-greenwash. Quote/depth **is** the last-arg correctness class; heap slice is already in tree.

### I3 — Shared **ident-slice** helper; apply to **7.10 leftover concat** ⭐
**Shape:** One tiny helper in `c_emit_secret.oo` or `c_emit_args.oo` (already imported):

- `c_ident_end(src, start) -> Int` **or** `c_slice_ident_at(src, start) -> String`
- Start/cont class **once** (kill the 70-line `is_al` copy in `c_parse_secret_env`)
- **7.10:** replace `name = name + c` with `name = str_slice(src, name_start, k)` — **this is the remaining leak**
- **7.2:** do **not** rewrite last-arg with the ident helper (wrong span type). Last-arg already sliced.
- **7.1:** already sliced; optional call-site swap only if zero behavior change

**Minimal path-A:** no new package. 7.10 name loop is the only **required** rewrite.

**Smoke:** existing `secret_invalid_empty.oo` + `secret_midline_safe.oo` + one `// SECRET: longish_name` still tags; I2 last-arg matrix must not regress.
**Darwin:** Close 8 · Honest 9 · Smoke 8 · Entropy 9 · Ship 8 → **avg 8.4**
**Why ship-with-winner:** 7.2 itself is slice-correct; helper **closes 7.10** with the 7.1/7.2 pattern and stops the next agent from “fixing” last-arg via concat or a fake C buffer.

### I4 — Shared **quote + depth** skip (`c_skip_c_quote` / `c_top_comma`)
**Shape:** Extract the in-string / escape / `(`/`)` step used by `c_sys_exec_last_arg` and `c_count_top_args`. Optional later: feed `c_args_drop_first` the same skip (it is **not** string-aware today).

**Darwin:** Close 4 · Honest 8 · Smoke 5 · Entropy 7 · Ship 6 → **avg 6.0**
**Why later hygiene:** Lowers copy-paste drift; does **not** close 7.2 (already sliced) or 7.10 (ident concat). Same-wave only if line budget after I1+I2. Do **not** invent a generic C re-lexer.

### I5 — Make `c_args_drop_first` string-aware
**Shape:** Same quote skip as last-arg so `write_file(fs, "a,b", content)` does not drop at the inner comma. Emit uses this for `sys_exec` rest argv (`c_emit_lower.oo`).

**Darwin:** Close 5 · Honest 8 · Smoke 6 · Entropy 6 · Ship 5 → **avg 6.0**
**Why later (adjacent):** Real emit-correctness; **not** the 7.2 CRIT. Name as residual if quote/depth smoke on **sys_exec rest** shows a split. Do not fold into 7.2 “FIXED” claim.

### I6 — Last-arg scans **all** argv idents (drop token walk)
**Shape:** Walk every top-level span, slice each, refuse SECRET idents. Delete or ignore `c_secret_scan_call` for sys_exec.

**Darwin:** Close 5 · Honest 4 · Smoke 4 · Entropy 3 · Ship 3 → **avg 3.8**
**Why not now:** Re-implements T2 token walk in C-text. Mid-argv already covered (`secret_sys_exec_argv_fail`). Scope creep past 7.2 heap close. Dual-path drop is FN risk (same as s71 I2).

### I7 — Token-stream last-arg (pass toks into emit guard)
**Shape:** Last IDENT from lexer instead of C-text slice.

**Darwin:** Close 6 · Honest 7 · Smoke 4 · Entropy 4 · Ship 2 → **avg 4.6**
**Why later:** Signature change across emit-lower/call. Does **not** fix 7.2 heap (already sliced). Architecture-adjacent; s71 I3 twin.

### I8 — Literal SPRINT: C stack buffer for last span
**Shape:** Lower walker to C `char buf[N]` / `chs_rt` helper.
**Darwin:** Close 3 · Honest 1 · Smoke 2 · Entropy 0 · Ship 1 → **avg 1.4 — DISQUALIFIED**
**Why dies:** Wrong language layer. `t1_memory.oot` already rejected this for 7.1/7.2.

### I9 — Full AST argv lattice / IFC
**Shape:** Typed arg nodes; no C-text last-arg.
**Darwin:** Close 6 · Honest 4 · Smoke 1 · Entropy 0 · Ship 0 → **avg 2.2 — REJECT**
**Why dies:** Moonshot. Out of residual 7.2.

### I10 — Naive `contains` / last-comma `split` without quote skip
**Shape:** `rsplit` on `,` or grep last token.
**Darwin:** Close 2 · Honest 0 · Smoke 1 · Entropy 0 · Ship 6 → **avg 1.8 — DISQUALIFIED**
**Why dies:** Quote/depth FN+FP. Undoes the whole point of the existing walker.

### I11 — Doc-only: “7.2 already sliced” without smoke
**Shape:** Flip SPRINT from comments.
**Darwin:** Close 3 · Honest 4 · Smoke 0 · Entropy 2 · Ship 9 → **avg 3.6**
**Why not alone:** Greenwash. Honesty line **belongs inside I1+I2**, not as the close.


